  "tutorial.step.artifact.body": "The Artifact tab is the optimized output. Inspect the final prompt, tuned ReAct tools, rewritten Flex code, or optimized workflow nodes. Download the runnable DSPy program, a pickle when available, prompt JSON, optimized Python, or logs CSV from the export menu.",
  "tutorial.step.artifact.title": "Inspect and export the result",
  "tutorial.step.code.body": "The Code tab preserves what went into the run. A single-module run shows its Signature and metric; a workflow run shows the compiled DSPy program, metric, and read-only graph. The optimized output lives separately in Artifact.",
  "tutorial.step.code.title": "Source and workflow code",
  "tutorial.step.dataset_library.body": "Upload CSV, JSON, or Excel once and reuse it everywhere. Search the library, inspect rows and linked optimizations, edit in the sheet with autosave and undo, share viewer or editor access, or clone a dataset shared with you into your own library.",
  "tutorial.step.dataset_library.title": "Reusable dataset library",
  "tutorial.step.model_billing.body": "Choose the billing source separately for every model. Skynet Credits cover provider usage; BYOK uses your verified provider key and charges only the small platform fee in credits. The same dialog also sets reasoning effort, temperature, and maximum output tokens.",
  "tutorial.step.model_billing.title": "Credits or your own key",
  "tutorial.step.react_tools.body": "ReAct is for tasks that need tools. Choose the allowed tool sources and iteration limit here; approval rules still apply at runtime. In the Usage tab, Skynet renders reasoning, actions, observations, and the final answer as structured activity.",
  "tutorial.step.react_tools.title": "Configure a ReAct agent",
  "tutorial.step.result_actions.body": "Share a run with viewer or editor access, or create a link for either role. Clone starts a new submission from the same setup. The matching sidebar menu also contains rename, pin, and delete actions.",
  "tutorial.step.result_actions.title": "Share or reuse a run",
  "tutorial.step.settings_billing.body": "Billing shows your real credit balance, lets you add credits, and keeps Stripe-backed billing details and masked payment methods. Transaction history sits below saved payment methods. Usage is a separate tab with model and run breakdowns plus export.",
  "tutorial.step.settings_billing.title": "Billing and transactions",
  "tutorial.step.settings_navigation.body": "Settings also lets you set defaults for the wizard, tagger, and agent; choose language and display preferences; manage passkeys, two-factor sign-in, API tokens, and storage; and open About. Use About to send private-beta feedback whenever something is confusing or missing.",
  "tutorial.step.settings_navigation.title": "Your control center",
  "tutorial.step.settings_privacy.body": "Choose whether Skynet emails you about optimization progress and sharing changes. This tab also controls product analytics, clears local cache, exports your account data, and permanently deletes the account when requested.",
  "tutorial.step.settings_privacy.title": "Notifications and privacy",
  "tutorial.step.settings_providers.body": "Save and verify a provider key once; the secret is encrypted and only a masked version returns to the browser. After verification, switch any model picker to BYOK and choose models available through that connection.",
  "tutorial.step.settings_providers.title": "Manage BYOK providers",
  "tutorial.step.workflow_canvas.body": "Use Workflow when the task needs several connected steps. Build the graph manually or ask the code agent to create and revise it, configure each node, attach tools where needed, and dry-run sample input before submission.",
  "tutorial.step.workflow_canvas.title": "Build a multi-step workflow",
