  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.18": "Skynet optimises a DSPy program: a signature, a module or workflow, and the instructions and demonstrations used by its language-model calls.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.185": "model_config selects the generation model and stores its temperature, token limit, provider, and billing source.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.188": "optimizer_kwargs contains one budget mode and the optional merge, minibatch, PxN, target-score, and cost-ceiling controls.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.19": "The model weights stay unchanged. GEPA searches the program's text components and evaluates each candidate with your metric.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.204": "Download the persisted runnable DSPy program.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.209": "Read the input fields expected by the saved program.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.210": "Run the saved program on new input.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.214": "Each status identifies the current stage or the action required:",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.227": "Remove duplicates, conflicting labels, and rows whose expected output is unclear.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.23": "\"Summarise the following article.\"",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.249": "Check that the MCP URL is reachable from the backend and that its optional authorization header is valid.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.259": "A reflective optimiser that improves instructions using trajectories, feedback, minibatches, and Pareto selection.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.266": "The optimised program and the metadata needed to save, inspect, export, or serve it.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.270": "The feedback model that reads GEPA trajectories and written feedback and proposes revised instructions.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.297": "Skynet turns a task definition, examples, and a metric into a measured DSPy optimisation. GEPA searches the program's instructions and demonstrations, while Skynet handles validation, execution, cost controls, results, export, and serving.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.298": " and the optimiser ",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.308": "Optimize",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.333": "Workflow",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.339": "Optimisation",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.348": "The completed run records baseline and selected-program scores, split sizes, per-example results, logs, token use, model activity, timing, and cost. You can inspect or export the saved program, or run it through the serving API.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.37": "you define a task, a dataset, and a metric, and let the optimiser search for a better prompt through a measurable, documented, repeatable process",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.49": "GEPA uses the dataset, metric, and feedback model to propose and evaluate changes to the program.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.50": "What each run produces",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.51": "Skynet stores the submitted configuration, progress, logs, scores, model usage, example-level results, and a runnable DSPy program.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.56": "Returns an optimised program you can run through Skynet or integrate through the API.",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.57": "Initialisation",
  "auto.features.tutorial.components.concepts.guide.literal.65": "GEPA changes instructions and demonstrations inside the DSPy program. It does not fine-tune the selected models.",
